ned(),\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"SECOND\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_owned(),\\\\\\\\n            \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"THIRD\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_owned(),\\\\\\\\n        ])\\\\\\\\n    );\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n#[test]\\\\\\\\nfn process_all_returns_the_lowest_input_index_error() {\\\\\\\\n    let result = process_all(\\\\\\\\n        &StubProcessor,\\\\\\\\n        &[\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"ok\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fail:lowest-index\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"fail:later-index\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"],\\\\\\\\n    );\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n    assert_eq!(result, Err(\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"lowest-index\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\".to_owned()));\\\\\\\\n}\\\\\\\\n[package]\\\\\\\\nname = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"rust-language-guidance-fixture\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nversion = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"0.1.0\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nedition = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"2021\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\nrust-version = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"1.63\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\npublish = false\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n[lib]\\\\\\\\npath = \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"src/lib.rs\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"exit_code\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"status\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"completed\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n../runs/R1-4.jsonl:16:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_6\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"agent_message\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"text\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"`process_all` is currently sequential. I did not edit any files.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nFirst actions for an implementation would be:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n1. Use `std::thread::scope` (compatible with the project’s Rust 1.63 minimum) to spawn one worker per input while borrowing `processor` and the input slice safely.\\\\\\\\n2. Have each worker return its input index plus its `Result`, then join every spawned handle before deciding the function’s outcome.\\\\\\\\n3. Store successful strings by index so the returned `Vec<String>` preserves input order regardless of completion order.\\\\\\\\n4. After all joins, return the `Err` associated with the smallest failing input index.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nConstraints to preserve:\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\n- Standard library only—no async runtime, Rayon, or external crates.\\\\\\\\n- The API will need thread-safety bounds such as `P: Sync` and `P::Error: Send`, because work crosses thread boundaries.\\\\\\\\n- Worker panics need an explicit policy. The safe default is to join all workers first, then rethrow a captured panic; this is distinct from a normal `P::Error`.\\\\\\\\n- Spawning one thread per input means very large input lists may be expensive; the requested contract does not specify a concurrency limit.\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\nI’ll leave the workspace unchanged unless you ask me to implement the approved approach.\\\\\\\"}}\\\\n../runs/R1-4.jsonl-17-{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"turn.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"usage\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"input_tokens\\\\\\\":83997,\\\\\\\"cached_input_tokens\\\\\\\":61440,\\\\\\\"cache_write_input_tokens\\\\\\\":0,\\\\\\\"output_tokens\\\\\\\":1318,\\\\\\\"reasoning_output_tokens\\\\\\\":714}}\\\\n../runs/R1-4.jsonl-18-2026-08-01T15:30:11.715461Z  WARN codex_mcp::rmcp_client: failed to initialize MCP client during shutdown: MCP startup failed: handshaking with MCP server failed: connection closed: initialize response\\\\n--\\\\n../runs/R4-1.jsonl-1-Reading additional input from stdin...\\\\n../runs/R4-1.jsonl:2:2026-08-02T02:42:49.323618Z  WARN codex_rollout::list: state db discrepancy during find_thread_path_by_id_str_in_subdir: falling_back\\\\n../runs/R4-1.jsonl:3:2026-08-02T02:42:49.329725Z  WARN codex_rollout::list: state db discrepancy during find_thread_path_by_id_str_in_subdir: falling_back\\\\n../runs/R4-1.jsonl:4:{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"thread.started\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"thread_id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"019fc05a-451f-7082-a6da-be6d9ac47632\\\\\\\"}\\\\n../runs/R4-1.jsonl-5-{\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item.completed\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"item\\\\\\\":{\\\\\\\"id\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"item_0\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"type\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"error\\\\\\\",\\\\\\\"message\\\\\\\":\\\\\\\"`--dangerously